\name{ProjectBundle}
\alias{ProjectBundle}
\title{Create, open, and import an inspectable project bundle}
\description{Native R facade for a versioned local project registry. Registration records declared provenance; it never runs analysis.}
\usage{ProjectBundle}
\format{A list with \code{create(name, project_dir, purpose = NULL, raw_dir = NULL, metadata = NULL)}, \code{open(project_dir)}, and \code{import_zip(path, project_dir)}. Each returns a bundle object with snake_case methods.}
\details{\code{create} requires an existing project directory and refuses an existing registry. \code{open} reads without mutation. The returned object provides \code{set_data_scope}, \code{resolve_data}, \code{register_data}, \code{register_analysis}, \code{register_figure}, \code{get_data}, \code{get_analysis}, \code{get_figure}, \code{find_figures}, \code{set_design}, \code{get_design}, \code{get_condition}, \code{get_levels}, \code{get_selected_levels}, \code{get_reference_level}, \code{get_replicate}, \code{check_design_metadata}, \code{get_design_summary}, \code{summary_text}, \code{set_current}, \code{set_context}, \code{update_record}, \code{record_decision}, \code{rebind_external}, \code{save}, \code{check}, \code{summary}, \code{status}, \code{preview_export}, and \code{export_zip}. \code{set_design} records a versioned declared study design; optional in-memory metadata checks condition and replicate columns without reading a file. \code{get_design} returns the current or exact historical revision. \code{summary_text} and printing give bounded human-readable context. \code{status(compact = TRUE)} returns a read-only, JSON-serializable status bounded to 4096 UTF-8 bytes. By default it returns metadata only. \code{check_files = TRUE} explicitly inspects at most 100 distinct relevant file/code locators; \code{missing$unchecked} counts the rest. Ordinary getters report unknown availability until explicitly checked. \code{resolve_data(ref = NULL, purpose = NULL, verify, expected_scope = NULL, require_membership = FALSE)} requires exactly one selector and \code{verify = "sha256"}; it streams the selected file and rejects missing baselines or mismatches. \code{set_data_scope(ref, scope, reason, design_ref = NULL)} creates a DATA revision without moving current. Scope/design data require schema 0.3.0; earlier schemas remain readable. Clean save has no disk writes; meaningful saves preserve stale-write and atomic-publication checks. It does not hash payloads or probe URIs. \code{status(compact = FALSE)} is unsupported. Save and import writes are supported on tested local macOS filesystems.}
